// Q2.6: Can an array initializer by empty?
// A: No - An initializer must either match the length of the array, or be
//    omitted. It cannot be empty. (It also avoids the case of an empty
//    initializer {} begin confused with an empty statement block {}.
//
// ref: https://dthain.github.io/compilers-fa25/bminor

x: array [5] integer = {};
